  data: {
    LLM: "After the deal, dealer's left has first bid: each player states the length of their longest trump suit (five or more cards) or Pass; the longest length wins, and clubs beats another suit of the same length. The bid winner then announces trump. Dealer's left leads; play is clockwise. Players must follow suit when able and may trump or discard when void. The winner of each trick leads to the next. There are eight tricks; then each side counts card points in the tricks they won.",
    Player: "After the deal, dealer's left has first bid: each player states the length of their longest trump suit (five or more cards) or Pass; the longest length wins, and clubs beats another suit of the same length. The bid winner then announces trump. Dealer's left leads; play is clockwise. Players must follow suit when able and may trump or discard when void. The winner of each trick leads to the next. There are eight tricks; then each side counts card points in the tricks they won.",
    objective: 'Win tricks worth points. Reduce score from 24 to 0.',
    gameplay: "After the deal, dealer's left has first bid: each player states the length of their longest trump suit (five or more cards) or Pass; the longest length wins, and clubs beats another suit of the same length. The bid winner then announces trump. Dealer's left leads; play is clockwise. Players must follow suit when able and may trump or discard when void. The winner of each trick leads to the next. There are eight tricks; then each side counts card points in the tricks they won.",
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if able; may trump or discard when void.',
      'Six permanent trumps (Club Q, Spade Q, Club J, Spade J, Heart J, Diamond J) rank above trump-suit cards; then A, K, Q, 10, 9, 8, 7 in trump.',
      'Bidding: state length of longest 5+ trump suit or Pass; longest wins; same length clubs beats. Bid winner names trump.',
      '120 points per deal; rubber: count down from 24, first to 0 wins.',
