      "Turn-flow example: After the deal, dealer's left has first bid: each player states the length of their longest trump suit (five or more cards) or Pass; the longest length wins, and clubs beats another suit of the same length. The bid winner then announces trump. Dealer's left leads; play is clockwise. Players must follow suit when able and may trump or discard when void. The winner of each trick leads to the next. There are eight tricks; then each side counts card points in the tricks they won.",
